        "k": "p",
        "t": "A school may have one laptop or none. **Taking turns** is a computing skill: one person drives, one person navigates, and they **swap**. Nobody grabs, nobody laughs at a slow typist, and the next pair leaves the work saved. Two pupils fighting over the only mouse while a third sits unused have not yet learned the skill. Use pair work: driver and navigator swap every five minutes. The unused pupil joins as a **checker** who reads the steps aloud. Pair work uses a driver and a navigator who swap. Taking turns is a computing skill, not a punishment."
