        "t": "**Decomposition** means breaking a big problem into smaller parts that can be solved. 'Put on a school play' is too big; 'write the lines, make the hats, practise the songs' can be done. Computing problems yield to the same habit. A paper animation of a football match by Friday is not one job: one pair draws the pitch, one pair cuts the players, one pair plans the six frames, one pair writes the captions. Each part is tested, then the parts are joined. Decomposition means breaking a big problem into smaller parts. Test each part before you join the parts."
